  "id": "temporal-arteritis",
  "term": "temporal arteritis",
  "definition": "Temporal arteritis is an autoimmune inflammatory disease of medium and large arteries, especially those supplying the head, eyes, and central nervous system. It can cause enlarged, tender scalp arteries along with headaches, muscle aches, vision problems, and skin tissue damage.",
